course: dictionary
lesson: 9402
title: A spurt of something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spurt is a word with a few related meanings, and context tells you which one is right. As a verb, to spurt means a liquid shoots out suddenly and fast, like water from a burst pipe.
explain: As a noun, a spurt is a sudden short burst. «Then a coal slipped, the fire crackled and sent up a spurt of flame» means a quick burst of fire, not a long, steady blaze.
explain: Look for the words around it. «Children grow at their own speeds, with growth spurts that come especially in the teens» tells you a growth spurt is a time when a young person grows taller very quickly.
fact: To spurt means a liquid shoots out suddenly and fast.
fact: A spurt is a sudden short burst of speed, energy or effort.
fact: A spurt can also be a short gush of liquid.
fact: A growth spurt is a time when a child grows taller very quickly.
fact: Spurts can happen in spurts: a short burst, then a pause, then another burst.
exercise: «Then a coal slipped, the fire crackled and sent up a spurt of flame.» What is a spurt of flame? | A cold wind | A long shadow | A slow, gentle glow | *A sudden burst of fire
exercise: «Children grow at their own speeds, with growth spurts that come especially in the teens.» What is a growth spurt? | A kind of sports race | A time when a child stops growing | *A time when a child grows taller very quickly | A long rest after school
exercise: In a race, a runner finds a spurt of speed near the end. What does spurt of speed mean? | Stopping to rest | Slow walking | *A sudden burst of speed | Sleeping
test: Water that spurts from a burst pipe does what? | Drips slowly | Stays still in the pipe | *Shoots out suddenly and fast | Turns to ice
test: In «a spurt of energy», what does spurt mean? | A deep sleep | A slow drip | *A sudden burst | A long, quiet rest
exam: Which phrase means a time when a child grows taller very quickly? | Sleep well | A new pair of shoes | *Growth spurt | A long rest
